WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.310
Whaaaaat?!

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.730
But...

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.900
What now?

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.190
It doesn't seem like good news.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.490
As a matter of fact, the school open house
will be postponed for a week.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.660
--Oh no...
--For a week?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.290
Then it'll be on the following Sunday?

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.500
Yes. I was told that we should
postpone it for a week

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.950
because it'll take time
to reopen the road due to the rain.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.630
I do get that, but...

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.590
But of all days...

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.060
--Chika-<i>chan</i>?
--Alley-oop.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.850
What's wrong, everyone?
We can use that time to practice more

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.850
so that we can perform even better, right?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.480
It seems that she doesn't really
understand the situation.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.610
--Here's a question!
--What?

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.400
The Love Live qualifiers will be held on...

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.630
The Sunday after
the school open house, right?

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:05.330
But we received the news that the
open house will be postponed for a week.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.330
Yep, yep.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.330
And the date for Love Live qualifiers
will still be the same.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.970
Now, when are these
two events going to be held?

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.020
That's easy...! Hm?!

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.180
--Aaaaah!
--Hey! Pipe down!

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.180
Ow, ow, ow...

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.320
Are you two okay?

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.400
The same Sunday!

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:43.160
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.800
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.760
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:04.470
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:09.400
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.150
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:15.480
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:24.080
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.200
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.000
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:36.800
<i>Everyone laughs and cries</i>
<i>as</i> <i>they</i> <i>look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:45.220
<i>Because I'm sure the</i> <i>future</i> <i>us</i>
<i>will have the answer</i>

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:53.310
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.650
<i>We got dream</i>

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.910
This is where the
Love Live qualifiers will be held.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.910
"#3 Rainbow"

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.200
--There?
--It's in the mountains.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:10.000
It's been decided that they'll set up
a special stage for the event this time.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.330
So where's our school?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.960
It's over here, but there's no bus or train
that goes all the way there, so...

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.300
Then, how about going here first
and switching trains there, then...

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.510
Ahh! This is getting soooo messy!

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.220
We won't make it at all.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.980
We'd need to be able to fly to make it, <i>zura</i>.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.310
Then allow the fallen angel's wings
to transport you!

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.270
Oh yeah, I forgot we could do that.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.860
We will soar through the sky to the stage
on the fallen angel's wings, <i>zura</i>.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.200
It was a joke! A joke!
Use your common sense!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.030
--Oh yeah, <i>zura</i>?
--I see...

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.580
--You guys're doing it on purpose, aren't you?!
--Ow! That hurts, <i>zura</i>!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.920
Sis! Help!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.240
You're right! The sky!

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.960
Huh?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.640
Well then, everyone.
We have to go to the next venue, so...

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.510
It's been a while!

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.640
We'll go there by helicopter?!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.020
It's the future, <i>zura</i>!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.180
How cool...

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.560
It's like we're superstars!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.480
Why is Chika-<i>chan</i> the pilot?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.610
So... Mari-<i>chan</i>!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.940
Oh! That's our Chika-<i>chi</i>!
I forgot we could do that.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.110
I'll arrange the helicopter right away...

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.740
Well, you actually think I can say that?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:26.990
You can't?

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.620
Of course!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.580
I told my dad that we'd get a hundred
prospective students by ourselves.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.500
I can't ask for help now!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.670
Hey, you're stepping on the map.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.460
Whoops.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:44.220
Anyway...! Think of it as "all or nothing"!

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.390
So we can't do that, huh?

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.560
Ah! If the sky doesn't work,
then how about the sea?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.920
A boat, huh?

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.230
Ours is out since it's used
for business on Sundays.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.440
Then, what about you, You-<i>chan</i>?!

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.400
--Me?
--Right! We'll take your...

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.760
...dad's boat!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.820
Hello there!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.090
Full speed ahead! Aye aye!

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.370
Look!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:13.200
I am the light-blue wind right now!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.960
Come catch me.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.090
Hey! Why would I
say something so embarrassing?!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.800
--How lovely...
--Yeah.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.260
It's the future, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.300
Right?!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.180
To start with, my dad's boat isn't like that.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.470
So that won't work, either, huh?

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.350
--<i>Zura</i>...
--Realistically speaking,

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.680
there's no way for us
to be able to perform

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.980
in both the school open house
and Love Live qualifiers...

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.480
...except one.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.940
One...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.980
There's a way?

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.030
Yes. If we can sing at the qualifiers
as the first performers,

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.360
there's a bus right after that.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.790
If we can catch that bus,
we'll just barely make it to the open house.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.910
Really?!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:59.380
But if we miss that bus, the next bus
isn't for another three hours.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:04.490
In other words, if we aren't
the first performers, it won't work.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.800
How do they decide the order?

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.890
--Th--
--They're gonna do it by...

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:12.850
"Lottery"

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.520
Lottery?!

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.980
That's right. A rep from each group
will spin to determine their group's order!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:21.810
"Lottery"

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.770
That's a huge responsibility.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:21.810
Who's gonna do it?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.320
At a time like this,
our leader probably should...

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.860
Y-Yeah?

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.820
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.410
"Born on August 10"
"Today's fortune"
"Super bad luck" "Ouch"

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.160
The luck for a Leo today is... super bad.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.410
I'm losing my confidence...

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.700
Then maybe Mari?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.120
No. At a time like this, I think it should be
one of the original members.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.000
You-<i>san</i>?

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.580
Me?!

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.500
That's a good idea, <i>zura</i>.
She seems lucky, too, <i>zura</i>.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.050
Well... but is it really okay?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.510
Well, then... Let's start the lottery!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.320
Wait.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.600
Aqours has never been in a greater bind.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:01.350
Therefore, I, Yohane, legendary idol
of the fallen angels, must go!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.600
No, <i>zura</i>.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.360
Bzzzzt!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.900
--Why not?!

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.440
--Because you never win in rock-paper-scissors.
--Why not?!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:13.490
The other day, you suddenly tripped
on nothing and fell in the sea, too.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.370
We're always happy because
of you, Yoshiko-chan, <i>zura</i>.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.830
Don't tap my shoulder like that!
Don't call me Yoshiko!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.540
I've just been saving up my luck!
Just you watch!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.630
My true power
comes out during times of crisis!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:25.800
What do we do?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.800
If you are that insistent, then...

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:32.010
...play rock-paper-scissors
with me right here, right now!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.640
If you win, you can go.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:39.060
By the way, my fortune today is super good!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.140
So Dia-<i>san</i> checks it, too, huh?

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.280
A-Anyway, agreed?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.070
Well, then... Are you ready?

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.530
One...

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.970
Two...

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.000
Three!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.000
I-I won...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.790
This is amazing, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.550
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> won with paper, <i>zura</i>!

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:10.510
Hey! It's Yohane!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.630
And, <i>zuramaru</i>! You just
did something to me, didn't you?

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.890
I didn't, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.760
--She may actually do it!
--I know it was you, <i>zuramaru</i>!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.680
It wasn't me, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.100
--Okay. We'll trust in your power.
--It was you!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:21.810
It wasn't me.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.520
Now go and get the
glorious first performance!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.530
Fallen angel Lucifer...

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.490
...and my countless little demons...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.490
...bestow good fortune upon me.
Show us all your dark powers!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.000
Yohane! Descend!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.100
First performance...

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.610
First performance...

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.880
Twenty-four!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.560
Eternal life... Phoenix!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.940
This is no time to be happy, <i>zura</i>!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.110
So, what're we gonna do?!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.440
Number twenty-four?!
That's right in the middle of the event!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:15.950
It was our fate. That is what
the fallen angel's power willed for us.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.780
Slurp.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.910
I'm really sorry!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.580
You're not the only one at fault, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.170
But now that it's come to this,
we need to think about it seriously.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.510
Do we choose the school
open house or Love Live?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.420
You mean we need to pick either one of them?

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.170
We have no choice.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.180
If that's the case,
we should pick the open house.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.140
Yeah, we can't abandon our school.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.810
I know that's true, but...

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.190
What we need to do now
is to get many prospective students.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.230
Wouldn't Love Live be more effective?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.820
More people will watch it.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.650
We'll attract attention.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.280
That's true, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.450
Then what're we going to do?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.320
Who thinks that we should
attend the open house?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.380
Then who thinks that
we should perform in Love Live?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.710
We have to pick one.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.210
I know, but...

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.790
I can't decide, <i>zura</i>.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.300
Yeah.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:13.960
Chika...

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.930
It's just that both are important to us.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.180
Both...

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.180
are very important...

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:37.320
Ahh! I wish a good idea
would pop into my head!

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.650
Keep it down!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.490
But...

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.240
I do understand how you feel,

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.620
but we don't have the luxury
to think it over forever!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.310
Yeah, I know.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.610
Which do you think we should choose?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.340
Well... I thought I wanted
to perform in Love Live and shine.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.220
I wanted to see myself shine. That's why
I started being a school idol, but...

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.300
We were able to do that
because our school existed...

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.230
Because Uranohoshi existed...

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:04.910
Yeah...

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:09.800
Ahh... Why do they
have to be on the same day?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.730
I wish I had two bodies...

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.070
So, you still can't choose?

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.530
Yeah, it's hard.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.550
There is one other way, though...

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.710
Really...?! Whoa!

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.680
So, what is it? What is it?

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.850
In short, we aren't one person.
There are nine of us.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.810
Nine of us?

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.560
"School Idol C̶u̶l̶b̶ Club"

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.560
We split up?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.100
Yeah. Five and four.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:57.400
We split up and perform in both
Love Live and the school open house.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.280
That may be the only choice we have.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:02.570
--But...
--Can we still be called Aqours?

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:03.360
<i>Zura</i>...

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.960
Besides, I don't know
if we can perform well enough

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.490
to pass the qualifiers if there are only five.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.160
I understand that you guys don't like the idea, but...

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.280
is there any other way, then?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.210
I wonder if it is really okay...

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:21.220
It isn't... But all we can do is choose
the best option available to us.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.720
We can't perform miracles.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.890
We couldn't at the last
Love Live regional prelims,

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.000
nor in the case of the school merger...

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:35.900
So, we decide what we think is best,
then try our hardest to make it work.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.210
Alley-oop.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.360
I think that's how we are.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.660
Yeah.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.740
Mandarin oranges?

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.580
I didn't realize that they're
already ready to be harvested.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:55.220
Well, Uchiura's mandarin oranges
are famous for how good they are.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.090
--Mandarin oranges!
--What?

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.250
Mandarin oranges!

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.500
Chika-<i>chan</i>?

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.650
Mandarin oranges!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.390
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.010
"Love Live! Sunshine!!"

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.270
"Uranohoshi Girls' High School"
"School Open House"

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:11.850
Please come!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.690
Our school's school idols...

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.150
Aqours will also hold a live concert!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.770
Please come!

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.530
So, what did they decide?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.990
It seems like they decided that
they couldn't all perform here after all.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.740
Uranohoshi students couldn't be here
either because of the open house.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:33.910
It might be pretty tough this time.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.310
So, we should cheer hard enough
to make up for it! Right?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.840
I heard that the first half has just finished.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.190
It'll finally be our turn soon.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.250
You'll be fine.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.850
Hanamaru-<i>chan</i> also said,

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.960
"If you perform just like you did
during practice, you'll be fine, <i>zura</i>."

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:05.780
And, the costumes you made for us
this time are so cute!

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.740
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.280
Wow...!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.790
Dia-<i>san</i>...! You look beautiful!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.580
It really looks good on you!

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.290
I-Is that so?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:21.640
I've always thought that you'd
definitely look good in a costume.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.670
Ruby...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.590
You have a very sweet little sister, Dia-<i>san</i>.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.430
--It's not like that.
--She really is my pride and joy.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.680
Now, time to go!

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.600
Let's make it to the next round!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:46.780
Contestant twenty-four! Here is Aqours!

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.550
--Girls!
--Go for it!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.210
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.730
Don't take this the wrong way!

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.940
It's just, we felt we had to be one, after all.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.190
Everyone...

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.150
Now, let's start!

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.940
Ruby-<i>chan</i>, this costume is so pretty, <i>zura</i>!

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.360
Now, let's do it.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.470
Okay!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:49.590
♪ Dance, dance! People were born ♪

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:57.260
♪ to become passionate ♪

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:14.070
♪ If the flames that are still small
and not burning very brightly ♪

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:18.790
♪ come together as one,
they will bring forth a miracle ♪

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:24.880
♪ To the heart that never gives up, this world  ♪

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:32.050
♪ won't give the answer,
but will give hints for how to find it ♪

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:37.300
♪ Let's be confident till the end ♪

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:48.020
♪ Dance, dance! Were people
born to become passionate? ♪

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:53.320
♪ Dance, dance! I'm sure that's how it was ♪

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:58.990
♪ That's why I'll dance as I dream ♪

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:04.290
♪ MY dance ☆ TONIGHT
(DANCING TONIGHT) Let's dance ♪

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:10.750
♪ MY dance ☆ TONIGHT
(DANCING TONIGHT) our best today! ♪

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.030
Now, let's go!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.570
We're not done yet!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.360
Are you guys ready?

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.610
--What?
--Next is contestant twenty-five!

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.200
--What's going on?!
--Next is contestant twenty-five!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.000
"Office"
"Grounds"
"Parking"

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.080
Let's go!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.080
Everyone! Hurry up!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.500
A-Are they possibly...

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.000
...trying to make it to...

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.670
...the school open house?!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.380
Mandarin oranges?

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.380
That's right! That area over there
is one big mandarin orange grove!

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.800
--So?
--So...!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.640
Yeah, that's our family
mandarin orange grove.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.100
All right!

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.180
But that still doesn't
change the fact that we can't make it.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.980
--Oh, I get it.
--Right?!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.190
Then, we go through here
to get to this side.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:15.190
--And then, if we go here and here...
--Chika-<i>chan</i> never gives up, does she?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.530
...we'll find a way!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.720
Come on, guys!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.920
Hey! This way! Over here!

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.800
Hey, girls. Wanna lift?

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.590
Thank you, both!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.010
I see... So this was your plan.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:44.850
This thing is pretty common on
mandarin orange groves. Now, hop in!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.140
Yeah!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.900
Hey, is this thing really safe?

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.230
Did everyone get in?

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.730
Full speed ahead! Aye aye!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.500
Even Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>'s
ideas aren't this crazy, <i>zura</i>.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.580
It's Yohane.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.210
I know, but this is all we've got.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.910
Can't this go any faster?!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.510
It broke off...

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:22.530
What?!

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.630
There isn't much time left!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:58.460
Can we make it?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.220
We're so close, but...!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.220
After we made it this far...!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.550
At this pace...

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.350
Are we really too late?

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:06.890
<i>Zura</i>...

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.890
I wonder if... a miracle will happen...

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.900
Here's what I think.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:21.510
No one tries to make
a miracle happen from the start.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:28.490
They just try as hard
as they possibly can to do something.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.590
They want to make it work.
They want to change something.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.770
It might really be as simple as that.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.500
So...!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.260
We can make a miracle happen, too!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.220
Can a miracle happen?

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:49.220
It will!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:50.720
Because...

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.100
Because...

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.160
...a rainbow appeared!

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:05.740
♪ Right now... ♪

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:11.250
♪ I want to try and change the future! ♪

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:19.040
♪ Because we've only
just discovered our dream ♪

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:31.390
♪ It doesn't matter what starts it ♪

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:37.310
♪ Let's go search for heart-pounding moments
together (Heave-ho! Excitement, all right!) ♪

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:41.900
♪ If it's something you really want ♪

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:47.490
♪ Then try and prove that it'll come true ♪

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:52.830
♪ I wonder where little old me can jump to ♪

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.120
♪ I don't know, I don't know ♪

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.340
♪ (It'll work out somehow) Ah! Let's start ♪

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:05.590
♪ Is your heart shining? ♪

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:11.180
♪ When I asked my heart, it said "Yes!!" ♪

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:17.230
♪ I wonder if our meeting
will change everyone? ♪

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:21.360
♪ The sun is shining on us today, too ♪

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:24.990
♪ Our dream
(Oh yes, heart-thumping sunshine) ♪

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:30.240
♪ Has awakened
(Oh yes, heart-thumping sunshine) ♪

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:37.960
♪ Right now... ♪

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:43.500
♪ I think the future is starting to change! ♪

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:52.430
♪ That's right, we've only
just discovered our dream ♪

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:10.450
We can't choose between the two.

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.740
We want to achieve both goals.

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:20.710
Wow...

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:23.710
So, let's move forward...

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:28.950
...in the direction that will
make our hearts shine!

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.680
Next Time! "Don't Call Me Dia-<i>san</i>."

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:41.570
"#4 Don't Call Me Dia-<i>san</i>"
